WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
Hawaiʻi, 2018.

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:06.330
Lava from Kīlauea pours
across homes and roads.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.030
About 800 million people live within
100 kilometres of an active volcano,

4
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.330
in 86 countries.

5
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.630
Yet the same eruption added new
land at the island's eastern edge.

6
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.310
Elsewhere, heat from volcanic
regions becomes geothermal energy.

7
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.850
Buried homes, new land, geothermal heat.

8
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.150
So is a volcano a hazard, or a resource?

9
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.210
In this mission, you'll sort
volcanic effects into four kinds,

10
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.790
from lahars to geothermal heat.

11
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.450
Then you'll travel from Colombia and
the Philippines to Iceland and Kenya,

12
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.450
and weigh the evidence.

13
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.210
Your mission: evaluate whether a
volcano is a hazard or a resource.
